 "text": "..title\nAn ordinance authorizing the granting of permanent easement to Piedmont Natural Gas Co. on certain property owned by the Metropolitan Government located at 2909 Sevier Street (Parcel No. 09402022900) (Proposal No. 2026M-091ES-001).\n..body\nWHEREAS, the Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County owns a parcel of property located at 2909 Sevier Street (Parcel No. 09402022900), part of which is shown on the attached Exhibit A; and,\nWHEREAS, Piedmont Natural Gas Company has requested permanent easements as shown on Exhibit A, across said property for the purposes of constructing, installing and maintaining a permanent gas line; and,\nWHEREAS, approval of the attached easement agreement is in the best interest of the Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County.\nNOW, THEREFORE, BE IT ENACTED BY THE COUNCIL OF THE METROPOLITAN GOVERNMENT OF NASHVILLE AND DAVIDSON COUNTY:\nSection 1. The granting of the following permanent easements to Piedmont Natural Gas Company across said property for the purposes of installing a new natural gas line and underground improvements to upgrade and improve service to the area (as shown in attached Exhibit A) is hereby approved.\n   Map - Parcel No.\n\t   Address - Location\n\t     Easement Type\n\t   Exhibit\n\t\n\t09402022900\n\t   2909 Sevier Street\n\t     Permanent \n\tA\n\t\n\tSection 2. The Director of Public Property Administration is authorized to grant said easements and to execute the necessary documents pertaining thereto.\nSection 3. This ordinance shall take effect from and after its final passage, the welfare of The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County requiring it.\n..Agenda Analysis\nAnalysis\n\nThis ordinance authorizes the granting of a permanent easement to Piedmont Natural Gas Co. (“Piedmont”) on property owned by the Metropolitan Government located at 4601 Murphy Road. This easement is for the purpose of constructing, installing and maintaining a permanent gas line. \n\nPiedmont agrees to pay the Metropolitan Goverment a total of $10 for this permanent easement, representing half of the fair-market value of the easement area.\n\nThis ordinance has been approved by the Planning Commission.\n\nThe Council Office anticipates withdrawal of this ordinance.\n\nFiscal Note: Metro will receive $10 from Piedmont Natural Gas Company, Inc. for the easement located at 2909 Sevier Street to install a new natural gas line. Piedmont will be responsible for actual physical damage to the land within the property and easement area and improvements and annual crops located on the property.\n\n"
